From 46ec47294894beb514eebb3ca853c788d9ba61d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:18:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02255/11362] [outer-loop] E3-in-agent validated end-to-end on
 cd82: pipeline works, induction quality is the bottleneck

Full pipeline fired correctly: collect (85 transitions, 1 winning) -> codex induce ->
VERIFY 27% -> plan_in_model found a 4-action plan -> execute -> DIVERGED at action 3 ->
HALTED (no solve). Two honest findings: (1) the E3 architecture works end-to-end AND the
verifier-grounding safety works -- it correctly refused to trust a wrong model (didn't
fabricate a solve, halted on divergence); (2) the BOTTLENECK is induction QUALITY: codex's
cd82 model was only 27% accurate (vs 61% on ar25), so its plan diverged from reality
immediately. Levers to raise accuracy: multi-round refactor (this run did 1 induce, 0
refactor) + better transitions + a stronger proposer -> directly motivates the open-model
selection + the refactor loop. Architecture proven; model quality is next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
